  "rationale": "PR #161 (anti-requisites) ships one symmetric exclusion pair in packages/content/data/cell.json: creo-ignem EXCLUDES creo-umbra and back, both halves reason \"destructive\" and resolution \"destructive\". That moves provenance.contentHash from d4e3047657b4fa8a1a74e1d52f9f5c86 to e8442af2c5f91ae6f80ad9a178e0e451, and gate.ts treats a contentHash mismatch as a block-level refusal, so all three gates reported baseline-invalid before reading a metric. The refusal was correct: the content did change. The repository owner authorised re-recording all three for this PR. THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BALANCE CLAIM: release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0, and nothing here is one. BYTE-IDENTITY IS ESTABLISHED BY GREPPING FOR NON-ZERO DELTAS, NOT BY READING THE PASS COLUMN -- a row can pass at 1.66 SE while moving 25.0, which is exactly what referenceGrimoires@permissive-breadth does in the agency gate below. NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED. balance-gate-ascension-v1 is deliberately NOT re-recorded here: it carries a superseded rngRegistryHash from PR #72, is already failing on main for that older reason, and balance/README.md marks its job not required to merge, so re-recording it is a separate decision on a separate failure -- the same carve-out the w70/opening-square notes record. THIS FILE (the twenty-year agency gate, worldTickCap 240, 64 runs, 8 strategies round-robin, 90 rows) IS THE ONE THAT MOVED, AND ON PURPOSE. The agency pool permits the full grid, so unlike the reference universe it can reach creo and the exclusion pair fires in a real run. 71 of 90 rows are at delta 0.00000. The 19 that moved are 9 pooled aggregates and all 10 permissive-breadth arm rows -- and NOTHING ELSE. THE OTHER SEVEN STRATEGIES ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL AT ALL 70 OF THEIR ARM ROWS; the pooled aggregates move only because they pool permissive-breadth. The headline: referenceNodesKnown@permissive-breadth 68.5000 -> 42.0000, delta -26.5000 (-22.35 SE against k = 3), and referenceNodesGained@permissive-breadth identically -26.5000 (-22.35 SE). Also referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter@permissive-breadth 15.3750 -> 3.75000 (-41.59 SE, the largest in the file), referenceKnowledgeInstances@permissive-breadth 1570.63 -> 990.250 (-7.67 SE), and referencePeakPopulation@permissive-breadth 323.000 -> 330.000 (+8.00 SE). permissive-breadth was the top-ranked strategy on referenceNodesKnown and is now fourth; its lead over passive-control falls from about +27.9 nodes to about +1.4. That is one authored pair doing exactly what an opposing term is for, aimed at the strategy that had none. Tolerances moved with the values, so balance/README.md power table is updated in the same commit; gate-power.test.ts is what enforces that, correctly.",
